  "question": {
    "text": "A vessel <math> <mrow> <mtext>ABCD</mtext></mrow> </math> of <math> <mrow> <mtext>10&nbsp;cm</mtext></mrow> </math> width has two small slits <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;sealed with identical glass plates of equal thickness. The distance between the slits is <math> <mrow> <mtext>0</mtext><mtext>.8&nbsp;mm</mtext></mrow> </math>. <math> <mrow> <mtext>POQ</mtext></mrow> </math> is the line perpendicular to the plane <math> <mrow> <mtext>AB</mtext></mrow> </math> and passing through <math> <mtext>O</mtext> </math>, the<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/6854.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 167px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rmiddle point of <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math>, A monochromatic light source&nbsp; is kept at <math> <mtext>S</mtext></math>, <math> <mrow> <mtext>40&nbsp;cm</mtext></mrow> </math> cm below <math> <mtext>P</mtext> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mtext>2&nbsp;m</mtext></mrow> </math> from the vessel, to illuminate the slits as shown in the figure alongside. After&nbsp;a liquid is poured into the vessel and filled upto <math> <mrow> <mtext>OQ,</mtext></mrow> </math> it was found that the central bright fringe is now located at <math> <mtext>Q</mtext></math>. Calculate the refractive index of that liquid.",
